In higher dimensions much less was known, until the recent paper of Beresnevich et. al. \cite{BerGuaMarRamVel}, who showed that, for $n\geq 2$, the \textit{Folklore set}
\begin{equation*}
    FS_{m,1}:=Di_{m,1}\backslash(Bad_{m,1}\cup Sing_{m,1})\, 
\end{equation*}
